CloudBurrow patch 72 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1585).

The bug: a division by zero failed "zero divided error ( 1.000000 / 0
)" (DIV and MOD "DIV: zero divided"), where GoogleSQL, and BigQuery,
fail "division by zero: 1 / 0"; and ERROR()'s error was its message
alone, which CloudBurrow's front could not tell from the engine's own
errors, all of which the emulator answers with reason jobInternalError.

The patch writes the division's error in GoogleSQL's form ("division by
zero: 1 / 0", the dividend in its shortest form; DIV and MOD
"division by zero: DIV(1, 0)"), and starts ERROR()'s message with
"ERROR function: ", which the front takes off as it gives the error
BigQuery's reason, invalidQuery.

